From: kodi-ps4 dev <dev@kodi-ps4.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:56:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] ps4: keep the glshim trace hook as a no-op

The glshim links WriteStartupTrace weakly. Define the hook without logging so the release build does not carry startup traces and the SELF link has no unresolved weak symbol.
---
 xbmc/platform/ps4/PlatformFreebsd.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/platform/ps4/PlatformFreebsd.cpp b/xbmc/platform/ps4/PlatformFreebsd.cpp
index cfda15874e..333d41d393 100644
--- a/xbmc/platform/ps4/PlatformFreebsd.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/platform/ps4/PlatformFreebsd.cpp
@@ -114,6 +114,11 @@ extern "C" int __wrap_pthread_create(pthread_t* thread, const pthread_attr_t* at
   return result;
 }
 
+/* The glshim links this weak hook; the release build does not trace. */
+void WriteStartupTrace(const char*)
+{
+}
+
 void PreparePS4Environment()
 {
   // The PS4 does not set HOME, the Kodi profile is kept next to the
